Cell["\<\
To summarize what I think is going on \[Dash] not sure I have fully dug to \
the bottom yet \[Dash] because of the relatively huge initial variance on the \
initial velocity parameter, it goes negative after applying the first \
measurement.  This means that when we predict the next state we are waaaay \
off.  (I don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t think the negative itself is the issue: it is \
1000 times greater in magnitude as well).   \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.941201989840811*^9, 3.9412020975703897`*^9}, {
   3.94120364789079*^9, 3.941203663552657*^9}, 3.9412036998870564`*^9},
 CellID->1177250074,ExpressionUUID->"f8cd2e35-1a02-4697-91a7-270567ecbf2a"],

