Cell["\<\
Takeaway is that process and measurement noise matters.  If you don\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t discount the accelerometer where you used the length of \
the club, then the model adjusted torque to compensate. Changing radius then \
didn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t help much.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.941297234169694*^9, 3.941297304172241*^9}},
