Cell["\<\
I found this link: \
https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2023/file/\
9dfcc83c01e94d02c751c47517855c9f-Paper-Conference.pdf which is interesting. \
It basically seems to be optimizing the measurement & process covariance \
matrices by directly optimizing the MSE between the Kalman filter\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s predictions and the desired output.  This is more general \
than  assuming the errors refer to random noise and estimating the covariance \
matrices, although they coincide under some assumptions.  I like this idea \
\[Dash] it seems to trade computation time for generality, which might be \
useful to us when using parameter optimization.  I wasn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t \
sure how to include parameter uncertainty in the noise estimates in that case.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.941300903294696*^9, 3.941300908927375*^9}, {
  3.9413015237845087`*^9, 3.941301639278368*^9}, {3.941301704589321*^9, 
  3.941301841999168*^9}},
 CellID->1417676410,ExpressionUUID->"1a8a0c7d-4800-451c-88de-6ef712aa06c4"],

